  "facts": [
    "Every timed traversal preserves the64-entry trace, dynamic query epoch, q-loop result weighting and ordered rotate/XOR block fold. A single checksum store consumes the full traversal; no per-value benchmark barrier was added.",
    "Fresh remains an outlined helper in both arms, called once per benchmark iteration. Inside its64-block backedge it selects shared law/plan, checks stride/overflow/exact extent (UDIV), checks plan/view unit bytes and one-code/non-hole admission, builds stack-local48B placement and24B predicate, then executes q queries. No allocation, plan construction or full plan-control copy occurs there.",
    "Retained loads its24B predicate by block ID. Reprepare repeats map/non-hole checks and pointer/code preparation once per visited block. The candidate outlines the reprepare traversal where R4 inlines it; this real call/frame difference is retained.",
    "One-shot repeats map/non-hole checks, plan/view pair and3-code-byte copies in each q iteration in both arms. Candidate additionally loads view->stride, compares to1 and stores the cached flag perquery.",
    "One-shot R4 stores the pointer-pair Q register once to the consumed predicate and separately copies code at offset16 with an aligned8B load/store. Candidate stores the pair to temporary and consumed locations, then LDUR W from temp offset47 (last pointer byte +3code bytes) and STUR W to consumed offset15. This overwrites the view pointer final byte; the shared checked filter immediately loads that pointer as8B. Exact addresses retained below. This creates extra copies and a concrete overlapping-store forwarding hazard; it does not prove the timing loss cause.",
    "The common outlined checked predicate filter remains real on every query, retaining coordinate/activity/domain checks, SIMD compare and sparse/strided/tail fallbacks. Full-tight path is54\u219253instructions; that count is not the strided path cost and cannot explain native timing by itself."
